package <%= basePackage %>.<%= module %>.domain.contract;

import <%= basePackage %>.platform.kernel.Command;

/**
 * Asks the <%= module %> context to handle {@code subject}.
 *
 * <p><strong>Rename me.</strong> {@code keel add module <%= module %>}
 * knows this context's <em>name</em> and nothing about what it is for,
 * so it cannot invent a use case. This is a stand-in with the right
 * shape — a command in, a result or a rejection out — and replacing it
 * with your first real use case is meant to be the first thing you do
 * here.
 *
 * <p>What is <em>not</em> a placeholder is the structure around it:
 * the command/result pair, the rejection this context owns, and the
 * fact that nothing in this module names another bounded context.
 *
 * @param subject what this use case acts on — deliberately anonymous,
 *     which is what a placeholder can honestly call the thing it was
 *     handed
 */
public record <%= Module %>Command(String subject) implements Command<<%= Module %>Result> {}
